From ece7ac889a78b26170798ad04634de4238d12918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco <mpalinar@nmblr.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:39:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Let the page cache serve repeated DiT block reads

The streaming path set fcntl(F_NOCACHE, 1) so a unified-memory Mac would not
hold a second copy of the weights. On this host the trade is inverted: 64 GiB
of RAM, and the same ~36 GiB of blocks is re-read once per denoising step.

Measured at 608x352 / 22 frames / 4 steps / 50 layers:
  DiT Euler denoise wall   151.2s -> 140.7s
  SSD stream               1.010  -> 1.186 GiB/s (142.9s -> 121.6s)
  unhidden stream wait       5.0s ->   0.2s
  total run                253.4s -> 242.7s
  peak RSS unchanged at 15.46 GB, swap still 0

Output bit-identical. H3_STREAM_PAGE_CACHE=0 restores the old behaviour.
---
 h3_gpu.m | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/h3_gpu.m b/h3_gpu.m
index 3acbc6a..a8348df 100644
--- a/h3_gpu.m
+++ b/h3_gpu.m
@@ -1010,7 +1010,17 @@ static int h3_gpu_tensor_read_file_bf16_mode(
         return 0;
     }
 #ifdef F_NOCACHE
-    if (uncached) (void)fcntl(descriptor, F_NOCACHE, 1);
+    /* Upstream reads the DiT stream uncached so a unified-memory Mac does not
+     * keep a second copy of the weights in the page cache. On this machine the
+     * trade is reversed: 64 GiB of host RAM, and the same ~36 GiB of blocks is
+     * re-read once per denoising step. Letting the page cache keep them turns
+     * steps 2..N into RAM reads instead of SSD reads.
+     * H3_STREAM_PAGE_CACHE=0 restores the uncached behaviour. */
+    if (uncached) {
+        const char *want_cache = getenv("H3_STREAM_PAGE_CACHE");
+        int use_cache = want_cache ? strcmp(want_cache, "0") != 0 : 1;
+        if (!use_cache) (void)fcntl(descriptor, F_NOCACHE, 1);
+    }
 #else
     (void)uncached;
 #endif
